3. HF AND THE TABLET IN THIS STATE
   HF: QMX USB and HDMI 5 V, 0.32 W at the battery (D); the QMX's own 12 V receiver is NOT powered in PS-IDLE-SPEC
   HF receiving is a PS-TYP load: 'QMX HF' 0.96 W at the load, 1.14 W at the battery (S: qmx-operating-manual-1_04_004.pdf: receive 'as low as 80mA' at 12 V; transmit 0.7 to 1.1 A (appendix 32.51 line 2816))
   The tablet: no row. It runs on its own battery; the kit's USB-C PD outlet, the one path that could charge it, is off
   in every state (pwr_budget.py: 'The outlets are off in every state and switched on only by the section 7.1 variants';
   contract 15 V at 3 A, 45 W). The profile keeps both functions in the kit at these duties; it does not power HF reception
   or charge the tablet

END. The budget's own figures, summed; nothing is measured.
